  "query_preview": "..Synoptic Setup: \nAnomalously strong upper ridging for this time of year moves in\nfrom the west over the weekend. This will lead to much warmer than\naverage temperatures next week. After a brief cool down tomorrow,\nhighs in the afternoon climb to the 80s on Monday. The remainder\nof the week looks to remain warm and dry as upper level ridging\nmoves east, save for any quick shortwaves along the mostly zonal \nflow.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nNo changes to NBM given the only model suggesting any precip is \nthe SREF. A brief shower in the east along the ND border is \npossible, but chances look to be decreasing.",
